title: Government Business
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/commons_1970s.jpg
tags: commons
view-if: whips_timer <= 0 and con_in_government = 1
on-arrival: whips_timer = 3; month_actions += 1

= Government Business

The Chief Whip brings the week's business. [? if govt_type = 1 : With a majority of [+ con_majority +], the government's bills will pass if the party holds together. ?][? if govt_type >= 2 : Without a majority of our own, every division is a negotiation. ?]

Backbench rebellion: [+ rebellion_disp +] out of 10. [? if govt_type >= 2 : Our partners' discontent: [+ partner_dissent_disp +] out of 10. ?] [? if bills_active = 0 : No major government bill is going through the Commons. ?][? if bills_active = 1 : One major government bill is going through the Commons. ?][? if bills_active >= 2 : [+ bills_active +] major government bills are going through the Commons. ?] The Politics tab shows where each bill has got to.

- @whip_hard: Crack the whip.
- @guillotine: Guillotine a bill in committee.
- @listen: Meet the 1922 Committee and listen.
- @partners: Keep our partners on side.
- @easy_discard

@whip_hard
on-arrival: rebellion -= 2; wet_dissent += 3; loyalist_dissent -= 2

The whips make clear that careers depend on loyalty. The rebels go quiet, and the resentment goes underground.

@listen
subtitle: -1 resource
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; rebellion -= 1; wet_dissent -= 3; right_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent -= 2

An evening in Committee Room 14. Nobody gets what they want, but everybody gets heard.

@guillotine
view-if: bills_in_committee >= 1
subtitle: Bills in committee move on next month. The Opposition and the Liberals will cry foul.
on-arrival: {!
for (var k of Q.bill_keys) {
    if (Q['bill_' + k] == 2 && Q['bill_' + k + '_amend'] != 1) {
        Q['bill_' + k + '_due'] = Math.min(Q['bill_' + k + '_due'], Q.time + 1);
    }
}
Q.lib_relation -= 2;
Q.rebellion += 0.5;
Q.wet_dissent += 1;
Q.guillotines += 1;
!}

The Leader of the House moves a timetable motion: debate in committee will end on a fixed date, whether every clause has been discussed or not. Labour calls it the guillotine, and spends three hours saying so.

@partners
view-if: govt_type >= 2
subtitle: -1 resource
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; partner_dissent -= 2; uup_relation += 4 if govt_type = 2; lib_relation += 4 if govt_type = 3

A road here, a factory there, a promise on the next bill. [? if govt_type = 2 : The Unionists want security and seats. ?][? if govt_type = 3 : The Liberals want progress on electoral reform. ?]
